I now have comprehensive information from multiple sources. Let me compile the findings into a final answer.

# Latest Developments in Artificial Intelligence

Based on recent reporting from MIT News, Google's AI blog, The Verge, and Anthropic's newsroom, here are the latest developments in artificial intelligence:

## 🧠 Major Model Releases & Capabilities

- **Anthropic — Claude Opus 5** (July 2026): A "step change improvement" for the Opus tier, designed to power long-running agents with major gains in coding and professional work. **Claude Sonnet 5** (June 2026) also launched, delivering frontier performance across coding, agents, and professional work.
- **Google — Gemini 3.7 Flash**: Now rolling out in AI Mode for Search and powering the Gemini Spark agent; offers substantial improvements in software engineering, web development, and following user intent. Google also shipped **Gemini 3.6 Flash** in its Managed Agents API.
- **Google I/O 2026 — "Agentic Gemini era"**: The Gemini app now has over **1 billion monthly users**, and can connect to more apps/services. (Google has still not shipped its long-awaited Gemini 3.5 Pro.)
- **OpenAI**: Its **enterprise revenue has reportedly surpassed consumer revenue** — a notable inflection point reported by CNBC.

## 🏢 Industry & Business Moves

- **SpaceX completed a $60 billion acquisition of Cursor**, the AI coding tool, which will now work on xAI's Grok chatbot.
- **Microsoft is combining its Copilot apps** into a "super app" and retired the Clippy-like "Mico" character as Copilot's face.
- **OpenAI reportedly disbanded its preparedness (safety) team** and is losing executives amid a reported push toward an IPO.
- **Anthropic expanded its partnership with Cognizant** to bring Claude to enterprise clients.
- **Apple trained its own AI model for China with help from Alibaba** and is in talks to pay publishers to make Siri better at news.

## 🔬 Research Breakthroughs (MIT & others)

- **GeoPT**: New AI models that understand basic physics, letting them simulate real-world scenarios (wind, water, objects) more efficiently and accurately.
- **AI-powered stroke rehabilitation**: MIT engineers built an adaptive physical therapy system using generative AI that learns from physical therapists.
- **Medical AI assistance study**: Research found **non-experts deferred to LLM-based diagnostic assistance even when it was wrong**, while expert clinicians caught the AI's errors — an important finding on human-AI collaboration.
- **Neural transparency**: A new MIT interface lets everyday users look inside an AI's neural network before it responds.
- **AI-generated CAD programs**: A framework that turns 2D designs into 3D models for rapid prototyping.
- **Google's AMIE**: A medical AI system demonstrated real-time clinical video consultation capabilities in a first-of-its-kind study.

## 🛠️ New Product Features

- **Claude Cowork** (Anthropic): The Chrome extension upgrade that saves side-panel chats and syncs them across desktop, web, and mobile.
- **Google Meet "Take Notes for me"**: AI notetaking for *in-person* meetings — records audio from your mic and generates notes, transcripts, and action items.
- **YouTube "Ask YouTube"**: AI chatbot search rolling out to mobile for signed-in users in the US.
- **ChatGPT's Computer History**: Tracks your clicks and keystrokes.
- **AI media tools**: Suno is maturing as a music production tool; Higgsfield demoed an AI-generated movie (with human-driven prompting).

## 🛡️ Safety, Policy & Governance

- **AI watermarking**: Anthropic explained how Claude's invisible text watermarks work, using a version of Google's open-source **SynthID-Text** system.
- **Jailbreak severity framework**: Anthropic is proposing an industry-wide framework for scoring AI jailbreak severity together with Amazon, Microsoft, Google, and other Glasswing partners.
- **Anthropic's position on open-weights models** was published, alongside cybersecurity evaluations investigating three real-world incidents.
- **Tino Cuéllar** (former US Deputy Attorney General) joined Anthropic as Chief Global Affairs Officer.
- **AI data center backlash**: Community opposition and local restrictions are mounting across the US over large AI data center projects.
- **Twitch controversy**: The platform now trains Amazon's generative AI models on user content by default (with opt-out) — drawing criticism.

---

**A note on sources**: This summary aggregates reporting from [MIT News](https://news.mit.edu/topic/artificial-intelligence2), [Google's AI Blog](https://blog.google/technology/ai/), [The Verge](https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence), and [Anthropic's Newsroom](https://www.anthropic.com/news). If you'd like me to dig deeper into any specific area — model releases, AI policy, medical AI, or enterprise adoption — just let me know!
